Q: Is there a better way to determine elapsed time in Perl? A: <p>This is useful for in-service timings, with a granularity of one second:</p>
<p>At the start...</p>
<pre><code>$debugtimer = time;
$debugstr = &quot;&quot;;
</code></pre>
<p>...anywhere and everywhere you like...</p>
<pre><code>kerchunk(&quot;message&quot;) # 'message' is a short description of the location in the code
</code></pre>
<p>...end of the program...</p>
<pre><code>print &quot;timings: $debugstr&quot;;
</code></pre>
<p>...and with your subs:</p>
<pre><code>sub kerchunk
{
    my ($msg) = shift;
    my $pertock = time;
    my $kch = abs($debugtimer - $pertock);
    $debugstr .= &quot;Elapsed at $msg: $kch&lt;br&gt;\n&quot;;
}
</code></pre>

Q: SetValues Formik Function disables Formik HandleSubmit A: <p>Turns out the issue was the is Validating Flag being set to true when you call setFieldValue so the simplest solution is to pass a third argument to setFieldValue to manually turn off validation:</p>

<pre><code>  submit = () =&gt; {
    this.props.setFieldValue('submit', true, false)
    this.props.handleSubmit()
  }
</code></pre>

