Q: Time calculation in Perl A: <p>An easy access module to use is <a href="https://metacpan.org/pod/Time::Piece" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Time::Piece</code></a>, which is core since Perl version 5.9.5. Constants for time math can be accessed via <a href="https://metacpan.org/pod/Time::Seconds" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Time::Seconds</code></a>:</p>
<pre class="lang-perl prettyprint-override"><code>use strict;
use warnings;
use Time::Piece;
use Time::Seconds;   # Used for constants ONE_WEEK, etc.

my $time_now = localtime();
my $time_hour = $time_now - ONE_HOUR;
my $time_month = $time_now - ONE_MONTH;

print &quot;$_\n&quot; for $time_now, $time_hour, $time_month;
</code></pre>
<p>Outputs:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>Thu Jan 29 17:20:55 2015
Thu Jan 29 16:20:55 2015
Tue Dec 30 06:51:51 2014
</code></pre>
